.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL = Element>
.br
class csmp::PointSource_lhsop< dim, CELL >"Assignment of scalar nodal (Neumann) source or sink terms\&. 

This operator applies (absolute) nodal source terms to the LHS matrix diagonal as they are\&. The nodal values must be precomputed elsewhere\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
the nodal term gets applied as many times as the node is a member of an element, i\&.e\&. n\&.Parents() times\&. Therefore the value should be divided by the number of parent elements of the node\&. This is already accounted for by the method \fBGetOperands()\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBDate\fP
.RS 4
12/5/2019 
.RE
.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
Stephan K\&. Matthai 
.RE
.PP

