.PP
Implements \fBcsmp::MathOperatorLHS< dim, Element >\fP\&.
.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class CELL> void \fBcsmp::PointSource_lhsop\fP< dim, CELL >::ComputeContribution (const CELL< dim > & e)\fR [final]\fP, \fR [override]\fP, \fR [virtual]\fP"
Applies point (nodal) source terms = Neumann boundary conditions to any kind of FEM models\&. The contribution is divided by the number of parent elements of each node because it will be accumulated by each one of of them\&. This is already done in the \fBGetOperands()\fP method\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIe\fP The current element from which the nodal values are accumulated\&. 
.RE
